{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":") makes a struct an event from its declaration. It is a product of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out, so only apps that use it build swift-syntax. It adds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformances, the event’s name, consent category and schema version"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you give them, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schema"},{"type":"text","text":", an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventSchema"},{"type":"text","text":" value that tooling reads:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3, coupon: nil))","let properties = CheckoutStarted.schema.properties.map(\\.name)  \/\/ [\"cartSize\", \"coupon\"]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The schema holds the name, the version, the consent category and each stored property’s name, its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type as written, its optionality and whether it has a default value, in declaration order. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoding writes each of those properties under its name, as a hand-written conformance does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property keeps its redaction. A record stored before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a property with a default value ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var currency: String = \"USD\""},{"type":"text","text":") was added reads it as its default."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"version:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" counts breaking changes only, and is 1 when left out; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","type":"reference"},{"text":" shows each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"kind of change. ","type":"text"},{"code":"consent:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sets the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"consentCategory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event(consent: .advertising)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A stored property whose type isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile error that names it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"static method 'requireBinaryCodable(position:)' requires that 'Coordinate' conform to 'BinaryCodable'","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"So are ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on anything but a struct, and a stored property without a type annotation. Static","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and computed properties are left out. The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Constraining properties","type":"heading","anchor":"Constraining-properties"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property’s type says what kind of value it holds; a constraint says which values of that kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are valid. A rule the type can enforce belongs in the type: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value satisfies every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraint of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the moment it is made. Rules a plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carry are declared beside the property with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker checks them:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum CouponCode: Refinement {","    static let constraints: [Constraint<String>] = [.pattern(\"^[A-Z0-9]{6}$\", example: \"SPRING\")]","}","","@Event(name: \"search_performed\")","struct SearchPerformed {","    @Constrained(.minLength(1), .maxLength(200))","    var query: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(0))","    var resultCount: Int","    var coupon: Refined<String, CouponCode>?","}","","let coupon = try? Refined<String, CouponCode>(checked: \"spring\")  \/\/ nil: UnsatisfiedConstraint.pattern","let tracker = Tracker()","tracker.track(SearchPerformed(query: \"\", resultCount: 3, coupon: Refined(\"SPRING\")))","await tracker.finish()","for await report in tracker.rejectionReports {","    print(report)  \/\/ search_performed: \"query\" breaks minLength 1 (1 rejected)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The keywords are JSON Schema’s: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minLength"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxLength"},{"text":" (in Unicode scalars) and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pattern"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a string, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimum"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximum"},{"text":" for a number, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minItems"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxItems"},{"text":" for an array. Each is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offered only for the types it applies to, with its bound in the property’s own type, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".minLength"},{"text":" on an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".minimum(0.5)"},{"text":" on an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":", is a compile error. In ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so is a lower bound above its upper bound, a pattern that doesn’t compile, and a pattern whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"example"},{"text":" it, or another keyword of the property, rejects. In a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"text":", those trap when its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraints are built. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"text":"’s plain initializer traps on a value that breaks its rule, as an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"text":" subscript does out of range; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(checked:)"},{"text":" throws the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsatisfiedConstraint"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Rejected events","type":"heading","anchor":"Rejected-events"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracker’s worker checks each event’s declared constraints before anything else, never on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"caller. An event that breaks one is rejected: never enriched, held by a consent, written to a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or delivered. Each rejection is reported on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker.rejectionReports"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"text":" naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event, the property and the keyword, and in debug builds it is logged at error level too.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Unread reports merge, one per event, property and keyword, counting the rejections and the range of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"times they were tracked, so a broken call site in a loop can’t fill memory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record that a store recovered from an earlier run is checked again, and the store forgets one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that a constraint added since rejects. A stored ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value whose rule no longer accepts it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t decode, and the store reports it. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property takes no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keywords,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"since checking one would reveal it; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive<Refined<…>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enforces its rule as it is made.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both kinds of constraint are part of the event’s schema. The exported tracking plan lists them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"beside each property’s type, and each example payload satisfies them, using a pattern’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"example","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},{"text":"). An array’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" elements are checked as they are made, but their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rules aren’t exported.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"},"metadata":{"title":"Defining Events","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"title":"Traffluent","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral anal